# sierra-hd: the deterministic mode and kernel-call trace (milestone 4).
#
# With SIERRA_HD_TRACE=<file> set, the SCI engine runs on a virtual clock
# (time passes only where the engine sleeps or waits), drives the music timer
# from that clock, seeds its random source with SIERRA_HD_SEED (default 0),
# runs the date and time from noon on 1990-01-01 on that clock, takes input only from SIERRA_HD_REPLAY
# (docs/formats/replay-and-trace.md), and writes every kernel call with its
# arguments and result to the trace file. SIERRA_HD_STOP_TICK and
# SIERRA_HD_STOP_CALLS end the game. With SIERRA_HD_SCREENS=<folder> (milestone
# 4b) it also writes the screen the player sees there, and (milestone 5) the
# 1x priority and control maps at the same ticks. With SIERRA_HD_ACTORS=<file>
# (milestone 5) every kAnimate call writes its cast there: position,
# priority, view, loop, cel and signal of each entry in drawing order. With
# SIERRA_HD_PARSER=<file> (milestone 6a) every kParse call writes its input,
# words, parse tree or unknown word and the event's flags there, and every
# kSaid call its spec and match. With SIERRA_HD_LAYOUT=<file> (milestone 6b)
# every window, text line, text box and size, control, inverted rectangle,
# menu, saved box and cursor change writes its layout there in 1x screen
# coordinates. In the deterministic mode (milestone 7) the AdLib driver's
# note ageing runs after each music timer call of the virtual clock instead
# of on the OPL callback, and with SIERRA_HD_OPL=<file> every OPL register
# write of the AdLib driver is written there with the number of the music
# timer call; with SIERRA_HD_MIDI=<file> every MIDI message and SysEx the
# SCI MIDI driver (MidiPlayer_Midi, the MT-32 path) hands to the MIDI driver,
# also with the timer call. In the deterministic mode (milestone 8) restoring a
# saved game takes its times from the virtual clock: the play time is set back
# to the save's on that clock, the wait and screen-update times are set to it.
# Used by tools/vm-trace to compare sci-vm with ScummVM
# (engines/sci/sierra_hd_trace.cpp describes the details).
